  "body": "Reported by the maintainer (filed by an agent), 2026-11-09.\n\n**What happens:** on the Setups page, picking a face for alignment is very hard: the pick keeps switching to an edge. Edges can't define a face-to-plane alignment the way a face can (the two-edge mode from #330 is the only edge use), so landing on an edge mostly gets in the way.\n\n**What should happen:**\n- The setup page's alignment pick picks **faces only** (no edge snapping), so clicking a face always selects that face.\n- The edge option is removed from the setup page's alignment. Other places that legitimately pick edges (operation geometry: contours, chains; MCP `pick`) are unchanged.\n- If the two-edge plane mode from #330 goes away, its command or tests are removed or refused by name, not left half-reachable. Record the decision.\n\n**Done means:** a UI test where clicking near a face's edge on the setup page selects the face, not the edge; the setup page offers no edge alignment; operation-geometry edge picking still works.\n\nRelated: #330 (face and two-edge alignment), and the three-point alignment issue filed alongside this one.\n",
